WEBVTT

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:36.650
When I open my photo book, I see different sides of me. {purichou...}

00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:39.420
Laughing, {warattari}

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:42.200
or playing it cool, in all the pictures. {sumashitari de...}

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.930
I don't wanna say, "what's with all these characters?" But... {nani kore...}

00:00:44.930 --> 00:00:47.640
Isn't this too much fun? {arisugi...}

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:50.220
For real? {maji...}

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:52.430
I mean, thanks! {tte yuu ka...}

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:55.760
Even if I lose my way,  {maigo ni...}

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:58.370
my heart's egg {kokoro no...}

00:00:58.370 --> 00:01:01.140
will be all right. Come back {daijoubu...}

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:03.830
to me! {modotteoide}

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:06.610
Hey, when we're together... {kimi to...}

00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:09.330
Hop, step, jump!

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:11.940
Because you're here... {kimi ga...}

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:14.590
Drew, draw, drawn!

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:17.460
I'm always with you...  {kimi to...}

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:20.180
Chip, syrup, whip!

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:22.860
One more time,  {mou ichido...}

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:25.470
unlock my heart! {kokoro...}

00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:28.240
I love you.  {daisuki yo}

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:30.700
All of you.  {minna}

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:33.590
I want to be next to you. {soba ni...}

00:01:33.590 --> 00:01:35.900
Okay? {ne...}

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:37.050
Love ya! {suki yo}

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:51.490
The second term starts today!

00:01:53.350 --> 00:01:55.610
It's the Guardians!

00:01:55.610 --> 00:01:57.350
Tadase-sama, you're so cool!

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:59.070
Good morning, everyone.

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:02.220
Rima-sama, you're so beautiful!

00:02:02.510 --> 00:02:05.720
Hinamori-senpai, you're so "cool & spicy!"

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:07.970
Same cheers as always, I see.

00:02:07.970 --> 00:02:11.520
It's rush hour on the popularity highway of their outer selves.

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:13.470
But everyone is really...

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:17.850
Like this.

00:02:19.390 --> 00:02:20.840
Bala-Balance!

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:21.770
Like this.

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:26.290
What should I do? Everyone's looking at me!

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:27.320
This kind of character!

00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:29.390
Ironic, huh?

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:31.910
Amu-chi, good morning!

00:02:31.910 --> 00:02:34.060
Good morning-dechu.

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:35.140
Hey, Yaya!

00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:37.690
Tadase, Rima-tan, good morning, too!

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:39.210
Good morning, Yuiki-san.

00:02:39.210 --> 00:02:39.850
Good morning.

00:02:39.850 --> 00:02:43.890
I wanted to see you over summer vacation, I was so lonely!

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:46.540
That's not true. Didn't we hang out all the time?

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:50.900
I was still lonely, lonely, lonely, lonely!

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:52.350
Fine, I get it already!

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:55.650
How am I supposed to handle you, acting like such a little baby?

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:57.700
Yuiki-san, you're so cute!

00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:00.100
I just can't get enough of that childishness!

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:02.220
Yaya-chan-senpai!

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:03.710
Hi there!

00:03:03.710 --> 00:03:06.920
That babyish character of hers is pretty popular.

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:08.770
It sure is.

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:13.930
Speaking of which, I feel like something's different about Yaya compared to everyone else.

00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:16.700
Rima-tan's cheeks are so soft and smooth!

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:18.160
Hey.

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:20.320
Even though she's also a Guardian.

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:22.060
It's strange.

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:27.060
Episode 48

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:27.060
A Request for Yaya!

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:31.520
Yummy!

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:35.190
Did you bring this chiffon cake for everyone today, Rima-tan?

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:36.830
Oh? There's one piece left.

00:03:36.830 --> 00:03:38.010
Gimme!

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:39.940
Why was there an extra....

00:03:40.750 --> 00:03:43.010
Sorry, force of habit.

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:49.000
I wonder if the Chairman is all right.

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:52.930
So, Tadase, what are we going to do about the Jack's Chair?

00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:56.620
The real Chairman is in charge of choosing Guardian members.

00:03:56.620 --> 00:03:59.050
Although, I'm a bit curious myself.

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:01.700
So for now it'll just be like a vacant position?

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:02.430
Yeah.

00:04:02.750 --> 00:04:08.810
Sanjo-kun's absence will leave a big hole, so let's try hard to work together, even more so than before.

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:09.350
Right.

00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:10.850
Roger!

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:14.060
And, although I think everyone has realized this,

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:17.850
the pure white egg we all witnessed...

00:04:18.670 --> 00:04:23.350
I think that egg is undoubtedly the Embryo.

00:04:23.350 --> 00:04:25.850
That's the Embryo?

00:04:25.850 --> 00:04:28.520
Well then, let's catch it, on the double!

00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:31.730
World domination awaits you!

00:04:31.730 --> 00:04:33.450
Prince!

00:04:34.630 --> 00:04:35.520
Prince?

00:04:36.350 --> 00:04:37.860
But of course!

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:41.020
We shall immediately capture it with a swift attack!

00:04:41.020 --> 00:04:46.970
Henceforth, we shall make capturing that white egg the most crucial of the Guardians' tasks!

00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:50.980
We will obtain the Embryo, and I will become King of the World!

00:04:50.980 --> 00:04:53.350
I shall be the King of Kings!

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:55.850
That's the spirit, Tadase!

00:04:56.150 --> 00:04:58.600
Isn't it a bit early in the new term to Character Change?

00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:00.830
Still, it's a pretty impressive character.

00:05:00.830 --> 00:05:02.720
You can say that again!

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:05.260
You seem full of energy and in good spirits.

00:05:05.260 --> 00:05:06.720
When did you...

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:11.640
Guess I don't need to worry about what's going to happen without a Jack.

00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:14.270
Right, no problem at all!

00:05:14.270 --> 00:05:16.690
Even the Embryo will be no prob-dechu!

00:05:18.490 --> 00:05:20.890
You are too naive, commoner.

00:05:20.890 --> 00:05:24.810
T-Tadase, this isn't like your usual Character Change!

00:05:24.810 --> 00:05:30.680
Someone as immature as you needs to put in some effort to be fit to capture the Embryo!

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:32.390
Huh? Effort?

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:34.390
That's right. Special training!

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:38.480
I'm going to work you to the bone! Prepare yourself!

00:05:40.720 --> 00:05:43.680
Everyone is just so full of energy. How nice.

00:05:49.380 --> 00:05:52.930
Ah, Yukari-senpai just went too far.

00:05:52.930 --> 00:05:56.500
She quit Easter without even telling me!

00:05:56.500 --> 00:06:00.220
Although, at least she handed over her data and materials.

00:06:00.220 --> 00:06:01.450
Chief Tsukumo!

00:06:01.450 --> 00:06:02.430
What is it?

00:06:02.430 --> 00:06:04.500
There's something interesting here.

00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:07.030
Transfer it over.

00:06:07.030 --> 00:06:07.780
Right.

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:12.290
Chief, over here, too!

00:06:12.290 --> 00:06:13.590
I'll transfer it.

00:06:18.930 --> 00:06:20.720
That's...

00:06:23.060 --> 00:06:27.360
I said it a little strange because I'd Character Changed,

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:31.720
but I just want you to do your best since Sanjo-san isn't here.

00:06:31.720 --> 00:06:32.780
Bye-bye!

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:33.440
Yeah!

00:06:33.440 --> 00:06:35.500
Hey, are you even listening?!

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:37.700
I'm fine the way I am now!

00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:38.570
Yeah.

00:06:38.570 --> 00:06:40.640
Special training? No way!

00:06:40.640 --> 00:06:42.220
Now now.

00:06:42.220 --> 00:06:44.530
You just said something that makes me sad.

00:06:44.530 --> 00:06:46.400
I made a special trip here, after all.

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:47.780
Kukai!

00:06:47.780 --> 00:06:49.030
Long time no see!

00:06:49.030 --> 00:06:50.690
Yo! You doin' all right?

00:06:50.690 --> 00:06:52.020
Kukai.

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:57.440
I figured Soma-kun is the perfect choice to handle special training, so I asked him to come.

00:06:57.440 --> 00:07:01.680
But why are you so adamant about Yaya doing special training, Tadase-kun?

00:07:03.190 --> 00:07:08.020
It's about time! You should come play with us more often!

00:07:04.700 --> 00:07:10.180
Yuiki-san has plenty of talent, but she always ends up relying on others for everything.

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:12.860
The goal isn't special training, per se.

00:07:12.860 --> 00:07:16.640
It's more of a way to push her to grow up a little.

00:07:16.640 --> 00:07:17.850
I see.

00:07:18.670 --> 00:07:19.600
But...

00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:22.560
Hey, hey! It's been too long, so let's go play!

00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:24.780
I wanna hear all about middle school!

00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:25.090
That might be pretty difficult.

00:07:25.090 --> 00:07:26.810
She's amazingly childish.

00:07:27.020 --> 00:07:29.490
Anyway, let's go to the Royal Garden!

00:07:29.490 --> 00:07:31.150
I'll make you some tea!

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:32.620
Oh, you will?

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:34.180
Soma-kun.

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:38.370
Oh crap, I can't let her take charge like this.

00:07:38.370 --> 00:07:40.430
Too late for that.

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:41.980
Let's do it, Yaya!

00:07:41.980 --> 00:07:43.140
Special training, start!

00:07:43.140 --> 00:07:44.460
Don't wanna.

00:07:44.460 --> 00:07:46.270
Well now, that's a problem, isn't it?

00:07:48.140 --> 00:07:51.460
Yuiki-san, we really rely on you!

00:07:51.460 --> 00:07:54.330
I think Yaya can improve more than any of us.

00:07:54.330 --> 00:07:57.260
Yaya's the type of girl who can do anything she puts her mind to.

00:07:57.260 --> 00:07:59.430
I sure wish I could see Yaya act all cool.

00:07:59.690 --> 00:08:02.170
Pepe-chan, why don't you try your best, too?

00:08:02.170 --> 00:08:04.810
You can do it, you can do it, Pepe-chan!

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:09.200
Well, if you're going to put it that way...

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:10.700
I guess we have no choice-dechu.

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:15.770
All right! First up is the traditional drag race dash!

00:08:18.610 --> 00:08:20.820
More like the "being dragged" race.

00:08:23.420 --> 00:08:25.520
No more.

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:29.250
Hey! There's no point unless you run yourself.

00:08:29.250 --> 00:08:30.470
But...

00:08:31.670 --> 00:08:33.780
Things aren't looking too good.

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:35.060
Um...

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:38.490
Did a parakeet fly over here?

00:08:38.490 --> 00:08:39.500
Parakeet?

00:08:41.150 --> 00:08:42.850
Now that you mention it, earlier...

00:08:44.890 --> 00:08:45.930
Bye-bye!

00:08:46.570 --> 00:08:48.430
What about it?

00:08:48.430 --> 00:08:51.430
It's the parakeet the third grade Star Class is keeping as a pet.

00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:54.930
It escaped when we were cleaning the cage!

00:08:54.930 --> 00:08:56.520
It was my fault!

00:08:58.390 --> 00:09:00.250
You don't need to worry.

00:09:01.390 --> 00:09:03.980
We'll find the bird for you.

00:09:03.980 --> 00:09:05.760
The Guardians will?

00:09:05.760 --> 00:09:09.390
Helping out students in need is what the Guardians are here for.

00:09:09.660 --> 00:09:11.610
Miki, Character Change.

00:09:11.610 --> 00:09:12.850
Okay!

00:09:13.390 --> 00:09:17.640
Someone who can draw anything well: Character Change!

00:09:21.400 --> 00:09:22.890
Like this?

00:09:24.240 --> 00:09:25.700
Wow, that's perfect!

00:09:25.700 --> 00:09:27.300
It's Pi-chan!

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:30.470
Hey, why don't we let Yaya handle this?

00:09:30.470 --> 00:09:33.570
It might wake up her hidden talents as a Guardian.

00:09:33.570 --> 00:09:34.760
Ah!

00:09:36.110 --> 00:09:40.060
Yuiki-san, do you think you could handle this case?

00:09:40.060 --> 00:09:43.390
Huh? By myself?!

00:09:43.780 --> 00:09:47.340
I'm really busy with the new term; committee meetings and such.

00:09:47.340 --> 00:09:48.480
Me, too.

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:51.290
What about you, Amu-chi?

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:54.060
You've got time, right?

00:09:54.060 --> 00:09:55.890
I don't know if I can refuse those eyes.

00:09:56.500 --> 00:09:57.940
But no, I must resist!

00:09:57.940 --> 00:10:01.490
As the Joker, I must concentrate on X Egg extermination!

00:10:01.490 --> 00:10:06.140
Aww, don't go bringing up that old excuse now!

00:10:06.380 --> 00:10:08.680
Yaya-chan-senpai!

00:10:09.550 --> 00:10:11.350
Senpai!

00:10:12.100 --> 00:10:15.140
Please find Pi-chan!

00:10:17.210 --> 00:10:18.560
I know, I know.

00:10:19.900 --> 00:10:21.270
That's our Yaya!

00:10:21.270 --> 00:10:22.770
You can do it, Yuiki-san!

00:10:22.770 --> 00:10:24.450
I'll do it tomorrow.

00:10:24.450 --> 00:10:25.950
Do it now!

00:10:30.140 --> 00:10:33.300
Hey, Mama, are you listening?

00:10:33.300 --> 00:10:34.750
I'm listening.

00:10:34.750 --> 00:10:39.140
Amu-chi and Tadase and Rima-tan refuse to help me out!

00:10:39.140 --> 00:10:41.500
So? Did you find the parakeet?

00:10:41.500 --> 00:10:42.970
Not even close!

00:10:42.970 --> 00:10:44.930
I searched all around, but...

00:10:46.930 --> 00:10:48.430
Hey!

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:50.930
It's not here, is it-dechu?

00:10:50.930 --> 00:10:54.350
I don't wanna be this "senpai" character!

00:10:54.350 --> 00:10:56.870
I just want to stay a baby!

00:10:56.870 --> 00:10:57.680
Now, come on.

00:11:00.580 --> 00:11:01.790
Let's go, Chappy!

00:11:01.790 --> 00:11:03.390
Okay, Sonny!

00:11:03.390 --> 00:11:06.110
We'll solve any case, right away!

00:11:06.110 --> 00:11:09.100
Legendary Detectives, Sonny & Chappy!

00:11:10.290 --> 00:11:11.600
Sis-sis!

00:11:14.170 --> 00:11:17.170
Tsubasa really loves you, Yaya-chan.

00:11:17.170 --> 00:11:20.850
He definitely knows that you're his big sister.

00:11:21.420 --> 00:11:23.350
Yaya-chan-senpai!

00:11:23.350 --> 00:11:26.390
Please find Pi-chan!

00:11:31.370 --> 00:11:32.500
There!

00:11:36.700 --> 00:11:38.770
Maybe I will try a bit harder.

00:11:56.440 --> 00:11:58.790
Yaya, what's with the outfit?

00:11:58.790 --> 00:12:00.730
Legendary Detectives, Yaya and...

00:12:00.730 --> 00:12:01.600
Pepe-dechu!

00:12:03.920 --> 00:12:05.340
Detectives?

00:12:05.340 --> 00:12:07.810
It was on TV last night!

00:12:07.810 --> 00:12:09.140
Let's go, Chappy!

00:12:09.140 --> 00:12:10.770
Okay, Sonny!

00:12:10.770 --> 00:12:13.300
We'll solve any case, right away!

00:12:13.300 --> 00:12:15.620
Legendary Detectives, Sonny & Chappy!

00:12:17.050 --> 00:12:19.880
And we'll also find that parakeet, right away!

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:20.940
Yeah!

00:12:20.940 --> 00:12:22.850
You're just mimicking them, though.

00:12:22.850 --> 00:12:25.820
Time to start! First, we ask around for clues!

00:12:25.820 --> 00:12:27.220
Right, footwork-dechu!

00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:27.810
We're off!

00:12:28.390 --> 00:12:31.020
I've totally got a bad feeling about this.

00:12:35.420 --> 00:12:37.520
Yaya-chan-senpai!

00:12:37.520 --> 00:12:40.580
What?! You scared me.

00:12:40.580 --> 00:12:42.930
Um, about Pi-chan...

00:12:42.930 --> 00:12:45.670
No worries! I'll definitely find her today!

00:12:45.670 --> 00:12:46.600
Just leave it to me!

00:12:46.600 --> 00:12:47.350
Yeah!

00:12:51.220 --> 00:12:52.470
Here's my ID!

00:12:52.790 --> 00:12:55.900
I'd like to ask you some questions.

00:12:55.900 --> 00:12:57.840
And what might this be about?

00:12:59.190 --> 00:13:03.470
Oh? So the Founding King's real name is Amakawa Tsukasa?

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:04.500
Yes.

00:13:04.500 --> 00:13:06.820
This is excellent evidence-dechu!

00:13:06.820 --> 00:13:07.470
But, but...

00:13:07.470 --> 00:13:12.930
Amakawa Tsukasa
Founding King
School Chairman
Planetarium Caretaker

00:13:07.470 --> 00:13:12.930
If you're the Founding King, the school Chairman, and the planetarium caretaker...

00:13:12.930 --> 00:13:14.430
Which is the real you?

00:13:14.430 --> 00:13:15.860
That's suspicious-dechu.

00:13:15.860 --> 00:13:18.150
Now now, would you like a cookie?

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:20.430
Don't mind if I do!

00:13:22.930 --> 00:13:25.730
She hasn't asked a single question about the parakeet.

00:13:25.730 --> 00:13:29.970
Why are we sneaking around like this?

00:13:29.970 --> 00:13:32.850
Because even though Yuiki-san is handling this case...

00:13:32.850 --> 00:13:35.720
We can't not get involved.

00:13:35.720 --> 00:13:38.410
But for the King himself to do such-

00:13:38.410 --> 00:13:39.530
Shh!

00:13:39.530 --> 00:13:40.680
Yaya will discover us!

00:13:41.560 --> 00:13:43.640
These are great!

00:13:46.920 --> 00:13:48.680
So this is the Embryo?

00:13:48.940 --> 00:13:50.130
Probably!

00:13:50.130 --> 00:13:51.680
I don't think it could be anything else!

00:13:54.790 --> 00:13:56.950
You should have also seen it.

00:13:56.950 --> 00:13:58.600
Why didn't you report it?

00:13:59.350 --> 00:14:01.600
Good question.

00:14:02.220 --> 00:14:04.930
With Hoshina Utau gone,

00:14:04.930 --> 00:14:10.100
you should realize that the task of finding the Embryo lies with you, Tsukiyomi Ikuto.

00:14:10.850 --> 00:14:12.640
I will no longer allow independent actions.

00:14:19.380 --> 00:14:24.980
I set Hoshina Utau free at your request, so you must work to compensate for her absence.

00:14:26.140 --> 00:14:31.170
Man, that guy pisses me off! One of these days, I'm gonna claw that old jerk up so bad-nya!

00:14:31.170 --> 00:14:32.350
Yeah.

00:14:33.070 --> 00:14:37.400
No matter how you struggle, you are still nothing more than my puppet.

00:14:37.400 --> 00:14:40.350
I won't allow you to cut those strings.

00:14:41.030 --> 00:14:43.870
I want a thorough analysis of all the data you've managed to collect.

00:14:43.870 --> 00:14:44.850
Right away!

00:14:47.790 --> 00:14:50.090
Pi-chan isn't here.

00:14:50.090 --> 00:14:54.100
Where could she have gone? I can't find her anywhere.

00:14:55.130 --> 00:14:58.390
Could this be a case of kidnapping-dechu?

00:14:58.390 --> 00:14:59.810
Kidnapping?

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:04.060
If you want the hostage returned, prepare one trillion dollars!

00:15:04.410 --> 00:15:05.970
You fiend!

00:15:05.970 --> 00:15:08.060
What a coward!

00:15:08.060 --> 00:15:10.060
So... So frightening!

00:15:10.060 --> 00:15:12.520
W-W-What'll we do?

00:15:12.520 --> 00:15:14.080
What the heck?

00:15:14.080 --> 00:15:15.180
Beats me.

00:15:18.650 --> 00:15:21.500
I-It might be the ransom demand!

00:15:21.500 --> 00:15:23.470
I'm scared-dechu!

00:15:23.930 --> 00:15:27.650
We can't pay one trillion dollars! Give us a break!

00:15:27.650 --> 00:15:29.060
Ransom?

00:15:29.920 --> 00:15:32.020
Mimiko-sensei?

00:15:32.360 --> 00:15:35.060
Hitsujita Mimiko's Ballet School

00:15:35.060 --> 00:15:36.810
Ow, ow, ow, ow, ow!

00:15:37.050 --> 00:15:41.700
Ah, Yaya-san, you haven't been to class lately, have you?

00:15:41.700 --> 00:15:45.170
All that time off has made your body become completely stiff!

00:15:45.170 --> 00:15:47.920
We can't have that now, my little fairy!

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:50.060
Just as strong-willed a character as always-dechu.

00:15:50.310 --> 00:15:54.660
Mi-Mimiko-sensei, have you seen this parakeet?

00:15:54.660 --> 00:15:57.260
No, I haven't.

00:15:57.260 --> 00:15:59.960
Have any of my little fairies seen it?

00:15:59.960 --> 00:16:01.340
Haven't seen it.

00:16:01.340 --> 00:16:02.910
I don't have a clue.

00:16:02.910 --> 00:16:04.840
No clues here, huh.

00:16:04.840 --> 00:16:09.060
Never mind that for now, Yaya-san. Make sure to practice a whole lot today.

00:16:11.310 --> 00:16:13.810
Man, what is she doing?

00:16:16.340 --> 00:16:18.870
Was that your stomach just now, Ran?

00:16:20.160 --> 00:16:22.570
Amu-chan, I'm hungry.

00:16:22.570 --> 00:16:24.060
What, you want to eat now?

00:16:24.060 --> 00:16:25.330
Just deal with-

00:16:26.290 --> 00:16:28.060
Amu-chan, was that...

00:16:28.410 --> 00:16:30.600
Crap. Right in front of Tadase-kun.

00:16:30.880 --> 00:16:33.470
No way! You must be hearing things!

00:16:33.470 --> 00:16:34.740
You're totally busted.

00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:37.700
Maybe we should go buy some food?

00:16:37.700 --> 00:16:40.520
It looks like Yaya's practice will take a while anyway.

00:16:42.140 --> 00:16:45.240
Yaya, hang in there-dechu!

00:16:45.240 --> 00:16:46.680
Yuiki-san.

00:16:47.330 --> 00:16:48.940
Mai-ti!

00:16:48.940 --> 00:16:51.930
Could the bird you're looking for be

00:16:51.930 --> 00:16:53.180
that one over there?

00:16:54.810 --> 00:16:56.890
Ah, there it is!

00:16:56.890 --> 00:16:59.680
Thank you, Mai-ti, Mimiko-sensei!

00:16:59.680 --> 00:17:01.950
Wait a moment, Yaya-san!

00:17:01.950 --> 00:17:04.950
My, what a cheeky little fairy.

00:17:06.430 --> 00:17:08.960
Come here! Here, here!

00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:09.480
Pi-chan!

00:17:09.480 --> 00:17:11.310
Let's play together again-dechu!

00:17:11.310 --> 00:17:12.640
Down here!

00:17:14.200 --> 00:17:15.640
Wait!

00:17:17.570 --> 00:17:19.600
Are you okay-dechu, Yaya-tan?

00:17:24.470 --> 00:17:26.030
You're not going to cry-dechu?

00:17:26.030 --> 00:17:27.490
No crying today!

00:17:27.490 --> 00:17:28.640
Let's go, Pepe-chan!

00:17:28.920 --> 00:17:30.310
Yaya-tan!

00:17:30.980 --> 00:17:32.390
Roger-dechu!

00:17:33.840 --> 00:17:35.770
Yaya-chan-senpai.

00:17:37.720 --> 00:17:40.760
When you're talkin' stakeouts, it's gotta be an-pan and milk!

00:17:40.760 --> 00:17:44.990
So cliche. They don't even use that in cop dramas anymore.

00:17:44.990 --> 00:17:48.250
We have kind of turned into detectives, though, don't you think?

00:17:48.250 --> 00:17:51.470
Tadase-kun as a detective? That might be pretty cool.

00:17:53.410 --> 00:17:56.450
I'm going to arrest your heart!

00:17:55.960 --> 00:17:57.470
Prince Gumshoe

00:17:57.760 --> 00:18:00.160
Ah, I want to be arrested!

00:18:00.160 --> 00:18:01.780
Amu-chan.

00:18:01.780 --> 00:18:04.960
Forget that for now. Yaya's gone.

00:18:04.960 --> 00:18:07.610
There she goes.

00:18:10.390 --> 00:18:12.770
I'm sure it flew over this way. Right?

00:18:12.770 --> 00:18:14.770
It should still be nearby-dechu.

00:18:14.770 --> 00:18:16.560
Excuse me, have you see a-

00:18:18.100 --> 00:18:20.310
Pi-chan!

00:18:27.850 --> 00:18:29.320
Kukai, look!

00:18:30.470 --> 00:18:32.680
There she is! It's Pi-chan-dechu!

00:18:33.680 --> 00:18:35.060
This time...

00:18:35.350 --> 00:18:37.910
I wonder where Yuiki-san has gone.

00:18:37.910 --> 00:18:39.930
We totally lost her, didn't we?

00:18:39.930 --> 00:18:42.450
It's because we went to buy that an-pan.

00:18:42.450 --> 00:18:44.710
We only went because <i>you</i> were hungry, Ran!

00:18:44.710 --> 00:18:45.270
That's right!

00:18:45.270 --> 00:18:46.550
Indeed.

00:18:50.410 --> 00:18:51.570
Yaya!

00:18:52.920 --> 00:18:55.460
Amu-chi! Guys!

00:18:55.460 --> 00:18:58.510
Why are you all together?

00:18:58.510 --> 00:18:59.530
Uh, because...

00:18:59.530 --> 00:19:01.970
Never mind! The parakeet is...

00:19:01.970 --> 00:19:02.850
Pepe-chan!

00:19:03.110 --> 00:19:04.910
Just leave it to me-dechu.

00:19:05.790 --> 00:19:06.560
Gotcha!

00:19:06.560 --> 00:19:08.060
Yeah!

00:19:08.560 --> 00:19:09.680
So close!

00:19:12.180 --> 00:19:14.370
Jeez. Fine!

00:19:14.370 --> 00:19:16.180
Let's go, Pepe-chan!

00:19:16.180 --> 00:19:16.580
Roger!

00:19:16.580 --> 00:19:18.170
My heart:

00:19:18.170 --> 00:19:20.180
Unlock!

00:19:20.180 --> 00:19:21.140
Yeah!

00:19:23.060 --> 00:19:24.270
Come on, Pepe-chan!

00:19:24.590 --> 00:19:25.470
Right-dechu!

00:19:37.080 --> 00:19:39.770
Character Transformation: Dear Baby!

00:19:40.020 --> 00:19:43.670
Finish this up at once!

00:19:43.670 --> 00:19:46.550
Merry Merry!

00:19:51.440 --> 00:19:52.560
I caught it!

00:19:55.450 --> 00:19:58.230
I wonder if they'll be happy.

00:20:00.400 --> 00:20:02.410
Thank you, Miss.

00:20:02.410 --> 00:20:04.590
Oh, it's you, Yuiki-san.

00:20:04.590 --> 00:20:05.530
Doctor?

00:20:05.530 --> 00:20:09.980
He's the pediatrician who looked after Tsubasa-chan when he was ill.

00:20:09.980 --> 00:20:13.610
You did really well catching Margaret-chan for me.

00:20:13.610 --> 00:20:15.750
Margaret-chan? Who's that?

00:20:15.750 --> 00:20:17.720
You mean this parakeet?

00:20:17.720 --> 00:20:21.030
Right! That's my Margaret-chan!

00:20:21.720 --> 00:20:24.290
No way, it's not Pi-chan?

00:20:24.290 --> 00:20:26.640
The markings on the face are a little bit different.

00:20:26.860 --> 00:20:28.720
Oh no!

00:20:29.990 --> 00:20:31.810
What am I going to do?

00:20:34.810 --> 00:20:37.100
3rd Grade: Star Class

00:20:37.100 --> 00:20:39.030
When it comes to investigations...

00:20:39.030 --> 00:20:41.900
Returning to the scene of the crime is standard procedure-dechu!

00:20:46.420 --> 00:20:47.310
No way!

00:20:47.310 --> 00:20:48.770
It's Pi-chan-dechu!

00:20:48.770 --> 00:20:50.680
Yaya-chan-senpai!

00:20:51.090 --> 00:20:53.280
Pi-chan is back!

00:20:53.280 --> 00:20:54.270
Wow!

00:20:54.270 --> 00:20:55.680
Thank you very much!

00:20:55.910 --> 00:20:57.310
What's going on?

00:20:57.310 --> 00:20:59.790
It's definitely this class's parakeet.

00:20:59.790 --> 00:21:01.180
Yo!

00:21:01.180 --> 00:21:02.160
Kukai!

00:21:02.160 --> 00:21:04.890
I see, the underclassmen did it!

00:21:05.700 --> 00:21:08.300
They're keeping quiet and giving Yaya the credit.

00:21:08.300 --> 00:21:10.920
Huh? Do you know something, Kukai?

00:21:10.920 --> 00:21:13.810
That parakeet was found by the third-graders.

00:21:17.370 --> 00:21:19.180
Kukai, look!

00:21:19.630 --> 00:21:21.180
That's...

00:21:21.180 --> 00:21:23.060
Pi-chan, come here.

00:21:28.690 --> 00:21:31.430
Did they not think Yaya could handle it?

00:21:31.430 --> 00:21:33.970
It's probably that they felt they had to help.

00:21:33.970 --> 00:21:39.060
Yaya's special power is making those around her want to pitch in.

00:21:39.060 --> 00:21:40.400
That's true.

00:21:40.400 --> 00:21:43.680
We were trailing her the whole time, weren't we?

00:21:43.680 --> 00:21:45.310
Now that you mention it, yeah.

00:21:45.310 --> 00:21:50.450
Borrowing the power of those around you is the first step on the proper path ahead!

00:21:50.450 --> 00:21:51.180
Yeah.

00:21:51.180 --> 00:21:56.360
Yuiki-san is accomplishing her role as a Guardian in her own way.

00:21:56.970 --> 00:22:00.300
Well, shouldn't we compliment her now?

00:22:00.300 --> 00:22:03.570
Yeah, she tried her best without relying on us!

00:22:03.570 --> 00:22:05.300
She certainly did her best.

00:22:05.300 --> 00:22:06.320
It was only so-so, though.

00:22:06.320 --> 00:22:08.020
Yaya was so-so! {this pun is untranslatable without a note, but this way keeps the joke partially}

00:22:11.700 --> 00:22:14.580
Did it come back by itself?

00:22:14.580 --> 00:22:16.600
We mustn't underestimate Pi-chan.

00:22:16.600 --> 00:22:17.640
No kidding.

00:22:35.760 --> 00:22:42.730
There's no limit to the dreams we wild things can see.  {abarenbou...}

00:22:42.730 --> 00:22:43.870
(Yeah, yeah, yeah.)

00:22:43.870 --> 00:22:47.080
If we're born with 100% possibilities,  {kanouseo...}

00:22:47.080 --> 00:22:50.030
then let's keep livin' at 100%. {hyakupa...}

00:22:50.500 --> 00:22:54.870
Let's cry and laugh, {naritari...}

00:22:54.870 --> 00:22:58.490
and meet all kinds of people.  {ironna...}

00:22:58.490 --> 00:23:02.030
Let's discover what's precious, {daiji na}

00:23:02.030 --> 00:23:05.040
and even lose it. {nakushitari}

00:23:05.040 --> 00:23:05.790
(But don't worry.) {hai donmai...}

00:23:05.790 --> 00:23:09.410
We've just gotta keep on runnin', {gan gan...}

00:23:09.410 --> 00:23:12.200
because that way's the most fun, you see.  {sono hou...}

00:23:12.200 --> 00:23:13.120
(Right on, right on.)

00:23:13.120 --> 00:23:16.560
I wanna do this, and I wanna do that too. {are mo shitai...}

00:23:16.560 --> 00:23:17.500
Let's go!  (Go!!)  {iku...}

00:23:17.500 --> 00:23:18.540
Move out! (Yeah!!) {susu...}

00:23:18.540 --> 00:23:20.780
Let's do it with gusto! {gachinko de ...}

00:23:20.780 --> 00:23:27.410
Because there's only one you in this world, {sekai ni...}

00:23:27.410 --> 00:23:34.570
you've gotta make sure you find the things you love. {daisuki...}

00:23:50.710 --> 00:23:56.190
One day, while walking around town, I heard the sound of a violin.

00:23:56.190 --> 00:23:58.470
The sound it made was nostalgic.

00:23:58.470 --> 00:24:02.000
Nostalgic, yet somewhat sad.

00:24:02.000 --> 00:24:02.770
Amu-chan, Amu-chan!

00:24:03.120 --> 00:24:03.890
Huh?

00:24:03.890 --> 00:24:06.270
Why are you doing the preview so seriously?

00:24:06.270 --> 00:24:07.930
What's wrong with being serious for once?

00:24:08.260 --> 00:24:10.330
Well, it's fine by me.

00:24:10.330 --> 00:24:11.810
Next time on Shugo Chara:

00:24:11.810 --> 00:24:14.300
The Secret of the Violin! Notes Dancing on the Wind!

00:24:14.300 --> 00:24:18.360
Hey, wait everyone! That's my part!

00:24:18.360 --> 00:24:20.100
Why you!
